      "text": "```\nHAND TOOLS vs. POWER TOOLS TRADITIONS\n========================================"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#023",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:woodworking:00-overview, git-history:woodworking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:woodworking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "woodworking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "woodworking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Woodworking: Wood, Tools, Joinery, and Finishing - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "HAND TOOL TRADITION                 POWER TOOL TRADITION\n--------------------                --------------------\nTiming: Antiquity → present         Timing: Late 19th c. → present\nCenter: England/Japan/Germany        Center: American industrial shops\nGoal: Surface quality direct         Goal: Production speed and quantity\n      from tool (no sanding)"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#024",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:woodworking:00-overview, git-history:woodworking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:woodworking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "woodworking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "woodworking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Woodworking: Wood, Tools, Joinery, and Finishing - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Key tools:                          Key tools:\n  Bench planes (No.4, No.5, No.7)     Table saw (primary breakdown)\n  Chisels (bench, mortise, paring)    Band saw (curves + resawing)\n  Western / Japanese saws             Jointer (face flattening)\n  Marking and layout tools            Thickness planer\n  Mallets                             Router / Router table\n  Hand router planes                  Drill press"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#025",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:woodworking:00-overview, git-history:woodworking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:woodworking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "woodworking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "woodworking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Woodworking: Wood, Tools, Joinery, and Finishing - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Philosophy:                         Philosophy:\n  Quiet; fine-tunable;               Loud; faster; consistent;\n  learned feel for wood              precision via jigs + fences\n  No electricity needed              Dust collection required\n  Better surface quality possible    Power can't replace technique"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#026",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:woodworking:00-overview, git-history:woodworking:00-overview]",
        "canonical_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "concepts": "[overview]",
        "current_path": "woodworking/00-OVERVIEW.md",
        "id": "maxim:woodworking:overview",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "woodworking",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[overview]",
        "section": "woodworking",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Woodworking: Wood, Tools, Joinery, and Finishing - Landscape",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Trend:\n  Hybrid shops: power tools for stock preparation (breaking down rough\n  lumber, thicknessing, jointing) + hand tools for joinery and finishing\n  surfaces. This is the dominant modern approach among quality craftspeople.\n```"
    },
